Fix the UABS and ULABS macros: without parentheses around the argument,
ULABS( xx * yy - xy * yx ) in FT_Matrix_Check() computes the wrong
determinant, so FT_Set_Transform() resets some reflected matrices
rotated by about 45, 135, 225 or 315 degrees to the identity.

Backport of upstream commit 05f343a64b1fc0ecd9d7e34d5510494cbe3b3793,
not in a release yet (2.15.0 is affected):
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/05f343a64b1fc0ecd9d7e34d5510494cbe3b3793
--- include/freetype/internal/ftcalc.h.orig
+++ include/freetype/internal/ftcalc.h
@@ -77,8 +77,8 @@
 #endif /* FT_INT64 */
 
 
-#define ULABS( a )  ( a >= 0 ? (FT_ULong)a : 0UL - (FT_ULong)a )
-#define  UABS( a )  ( a >= 0 ?  (FT_UInt)a : 0U  -  (FT_UInt)a )
+#define ULABS( a )  ( (a) >= 0 ? (FT_ULong)(a) : 0UL - (FT_ULong)(a) )
+#define  UABS( a )  ( (a) >= 0 ?  (FT_UInt)(a) : 0U  -  (FT_UInt)(a) )
 
 
   /**************************************************************************
